+The lookup backend is a local embedded SQLite index that runs inside the kiosk application process. There is no lookup service and no runtime network access; the HLD tenet that lookups complete using files on the kiosk is satisfied directly. Each kiosk validates and rebuilds its own index when a snapshot arrives — the cost is accepted because snapshots arrive by USB at the central inventory team's cadence, not continuously.
